## Routing

[React Router](https://reactrouter.com) v6 is wired up — `src/App.jsx` and `src/components/Navbar.jsx` are overwritten with routing-aware versions (same file paths as the base ships, so every other module's wiring into `App.jsx`'s provider anchors keeps working unmodified) that wrap `src/pages/Home.jsx` and a new `src/pages/NotFound.jsx` in `<BrowserRouter><Routes>...</Routes></BrowserRouter>`, with `Navbar`'s links using `<Link>` for real client-side navigation instead of a full page reload.

Add a new page:

```jsx
// src/pages/About.jsx
export function About() {
  return <h2>About</h2>;
}
```

```jsx
// src/App.jsx — add inside the existing <Routes>
import { About } from "./pages/About";
// ...
<Route path="/about" element={<About />} />
```

`npm audit` will flag a moderate open-redirect advisory in this version (fixed only in v7, which currently has its own higher-severity advisory in the data-router/actions APIs this starter doesn't use) — it requires passing untrusted, attacker-controlled input into a `<Link>`/`useNavigate` target, which none of the code here does. Worth re-checking before you add anything that builds a redirect URL from user input.

